From: Dodaskot <pessdres@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panfrost: allow two seconds for compute jobs

Valid long-running compute workloads on Mali-G57 MC2 exceed the 500 ms
watchdog. Increase the timeout to 2000 ms, retaining timeout recovery.
This is the sole source change in the tested kernel build #101.

---
 drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/panfrost/panfrost_job.c
@@ -23,7 +23,7 @@
 #include "panfrost_dump.h"

 #define MAX_JM_CTX_PER_FILE 64
-#define JOB_TIMEOUT_MS 500
+#define JOB_TIMEOUT_MS 2000

 #define job_write(dev, reg, data) writel(data, dev->iomem + (reg))
 #define job_read(dev, reg) readl(dev->iomem + (reg))
